      },
      "message": "feat(ui): drag a part along an axis with move handles\n\n#1198 slice b. The bottom bar gains a Move mode button; with it on, the\none selected part wears three axis arms ending in balls, a constant size\non screen. Pressing a ball wins over orbit and pick; dragging previews\nthe part sliding along that axis (view state only) and the release\nqueues one MoveModelBy, which the drain runs as the Model page's own\nMoveModel with the rotation kept bit for bit - one undo step per drag.\nEscape mid-drag and a zero-length drag add no history step. In a setup\nthat holds the part turned, the part moves along the axis shown.\n\nRefs #1198\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
